course: dictionary
lesson: 14599
title: Plywood: strong layers
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Plywood is a strong board made of thin layers of wood glued together. The grain, the lines you can see in wood, runs in a different direction in each layer. «Dad cut a sheet of plywood to make a shelf.» Here plywood is the material, the stuff the shelf is made from.
explain: Plywood is an uncountable noun, so we do not add an s or say one plywood. We say «some plywood» or «a sheet of plywood» or «a piece of plywood». Plywood can also come before another noun, as in «a plywood board».
explain: Because plywood is made of layers that go different ways, it is strong and does not split easily. That is why builders and designers use it for shelves, boxes, models and floors. «The stage in our play was made from plywood, so it did not wobble when we jumped.»
fact: Plywood is a board made of thin layers of wood glued together.
fact: The grain of each layer goes a different way, which makes plywood strong.
fact: Plywood does not split easily, so it is used for shelves, boxes, models and floors.
fact: Plywood is uncountable: say «a sheet of plywood», not «a plywood» or «plywoods».
fact: In maths, you can find the area of a sheet of plywood by multiplying its length by its width.
exercise: «Dad cut a sheet of plywood to make a shelf.» What did Dad make from the plywood? | A cloud | *A shelf | A paper aeroplane | A bowl of soup
exercise: What is plywood? | *A strong board made of thin layers of wood glued together | A metal bar made of iron | A thin sheet of clear plastic | A soft cloth made of wool
exercise: «A sheet of plywood is 2 metres long and 1 metre wide.» What is its area? | 6 square metres | *2 square metres | 4 square metres | 3 square metres
test: «Mum bought ___ to make a box for my toys.» Which word completes the sentence correctly? | plywoody | plywoods | *plywood | plywoodies
test: «The stage was made of plywood, so it would not split when we jumped on it.» Why is plywood a good choice here? | It is see-through like glass | It is soft and bendy | It melts in the sun | *It is strong and does not split easily
exam: Sam shares a 4 metre piece of plywood equally between 2 shelves. How long is each shelf? | 4 metres | *2 metres | 8 metres | 1 metre
